# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in the values you need.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored — never commit secrets.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public origin used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
# Leave unset to use the fallback in `src/data/site.ts`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://borhendkhil.dev"

# Optional. Enables the contact form.
#
# Any HTTPS endpoint that accepts a JSON POST with
# { name, email, message, submittedAt, source } works here:
#   - Formspree / Basin / Web3Forms style form endpoints
#   - A Zapier or Make catch hook
#   - A Cloudflare Worker or Vercel function that forwards to Resend/SES
#
# While this is unset, /api/contact returns 503 and the form hands the visitor a
# pre-filled `mailto:` draft addressed to `socialLinks.email` in
# `src/data/site.ts`. Nothing is faked either way: the visitor always sees which
# route was used.
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=""